    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n40770" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">rĕdundātĭo</span></b> ,
			ōnis, f.
		redundo, <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b><i>an overflowing;</i> hence, transf.: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">stomachi,</span>”
				<i>a rising</i>,
				 <i><span class="en">Plin.
					7, 6, 5, § 41</span></i>
			; <i><span class="en">11, 37, 55,
				§ 149</span></i>: astrorum, <i>the flowing
				back</i>, i. e. <i>revolution</i>, <i><span class="en">Vitr. 9, 1 <i>fin.</i></span></i>—</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>II.</b>
			<b>Transf.</b>, <i>the
			over-abundance</i>, <i>multitude</i>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">cicatricum tuarum redundationes,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Quint. Decl. 4, 11</span></i>
			.</div>
